# Local machine settings for the dotfiles installer.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/dotfiles/local.conf and edit it. That copy is
# mode 600 and is gitignored: it never enters the repository, and it is the
# only place machine-specific values or secrets belong.
#
# Nothing here is required. The installer has a working default for every
# setting, and a fresh install needs none of them.
#
# The installer reads this file as plain shell AFTER its own defaults are set,
# so anything you uncomment here wins. It is sourced, not parsed — keep it to
# simple KEY=VALUE assignments.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where Noctalia keeps wallpapers.
# Default: ~/Pictures/Wallpapers
# WALLPAPER_DIR="$HOME/Pictures/Wallpapers"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extra assets deployed to disk, referenced from configs as @ASSETS@.
# Default: ~/.local/share/dotfiles/assets
# ASSETS_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/dotfiles/assets"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The wallpaper the desktop starts with.
# Default: wallhaven-w5xokr_1920x1080.png
# Must exist in the repository's wallpapers/current/ directory.
# DOTFILES_WALLPAPER="wallhaven-w5xokr_1920x1080.png"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weather widget credentials.
#
# The Noctalia `weather` widget is present in the shipped config but is on a
# DISABLED bar group, so it is not visible out of the box. If you enable it
# (add "weather" to a live capsule group in config/noctalia/config.toml), your
# weather provider credentials go HERE, never in the tracked config.
#
# Read ~/.local/state/noctalia/weather.json after Noctalia has run once to see
# which provider it selected, then set the matching key below.
# WEATHER_API_KEY=""
# WEATHER_PROVIDER=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything else you always want overridden on this machine, as plain
# assignments. For example a package you always want present:
# EXTRA_PACKAGES=(some-package)
